# Cinematic follow shots + exports (2026-10-03). A follow shot's keys are the camera's offset AND view in the
# satellite's frame, so playing a key back gives the framing it was taken with (follow mode's aim is free; until
# this, keys kept only the offset and playback aimed at the satellite: a different picture).
#   f1/f3  key 1 taken looking at the satellite, then `path goto 0`: same camera (az/el/fov in the state files)
#   f2/f4  key 2 after moving the offset (the view stays put in the satellite's frame: the satellite drifts
#          off-centre) and zooming, then `path goto 3`: same camera, satellite off-centre in both captures
#   f5     the shot played (no Go to flight runs under it)
#   e*     a short HQ export and a preview export finish (App presents progress frames during the HQ one:
#          run with VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS=VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation and read app_stdout.txt)
observer lat=28.5 lon=-80.6 agl=50
time sun -12 setting
time pause
select const "International Space Station"
follow offset=-60,0,15
wait settle
cine new follow_test
cine shot follow sel
cine key t=0
state f1_key0
capture f1_key0 scale=0.5
follow offset=-30,25,5
camera fov=40
wait 2
state f2_key1
capture f2_key1 scale=0.5
cine key t=3
path goto 0
wait 2
state f3_goto0
capture f3_goto0 scale=0.5
path goto 3
wait 2
state f4_goto3
capture f4_goto3 scale=0.5
cine play shot
state f5_played
cine state
cine export hq fps=4 scale=1 frames=8 shot
cine export preview fps=4 shot
